From ed277f7417467fbec0eca8aca4a58b4fdc2bad10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:42:10 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] fix(sim): judge an upright tool within a stated tilt
 tolerance

The verifier's laws branched on the exact camcraft_cl::is_vertical, so a
pose 1e-10 degrees off the Z column (rounding noise from a rotated setup
or a posed operation) took the tilted reading: the reach law (c) dropped
a holder's bottom by its whole radius and a holder wider than the cutter
flipped to a false ShankHit.

One predicate, verify::upright::is_upright with UPRIGHT_TILT_RAD = 1e-9
rad, now decides "upright" for every verify law that branches on tilt
(reach c/c3, fixture bands/rapids c2/d2, posed steel, mesh steel, solid,
posed contact, posed-rapid second reading, all-air verdict). A tilt above
the tolerance, a downward axis or a non-finite one still reads tilted.
is_vertical stays exact, so CL dumps, posted output and goldens do not
move. Law (c) no longer reports the same ShankHit twice for one move when
a leaning shank and holder both reach the stock.

Fixes #938

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
